- **Breaking change:** Removed the `--team` flag from `fleetctl report`, `fleetctl user create` (along with its `-t` shorthand), `fleetctl generate-gitops`, `fleetctl hosts transfer`, `fleetctl run-script`, `fleetctl get reports`, `fleetctl get labels`, `fleetctl get hosts` and `fleetctl get software`, the `--policies-team` flag from `fleetctl apply`, and the `--delete-other-teams` flag and `DELETE_OTHER_TEAMS` environment variable from `fleetctl gitops`. Using one now fails with a message that links to the Fleet 5 migration guide. Use `--fleet`, `--policies-fleet`, `--delete-other-fleets` and `DELETE_OTHER_FLEETS` instead.
- **Breaking change:** `fleetctl generate-gitops` no longer accepts `no-team` as the value of `--fleet`. Use `unassigned`.
- **Breaking change:** Removed `fleetctl get teams` (and its `team` and `t` aliases). Use `fleetctl get fleets` instead.
